{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK13ReactorRouterV","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"ReactorRouter","roleHeading":"Structure"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ReactorRouter"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.event"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default:"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allow"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reactor handler is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, and collecting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" members by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at compile time, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade for the same reason."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signs no reply and interprets no ","type":"text"},{"code":"timeout_ms","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; its output is exactly the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Bind one handler per event and let the SDK compose them into the single","type":"text"},{"